    "badgeColor": "border-amber-500/60 bg-amber-950/80 text-amber-300",
    "title": {
      "en": "Character Caps in WoW: Forever, Cross Region Servers - Fiamma Interview with Clay Stone and Holly Longdale",
      "es": "Tapas de personajes en WoW: para siempre, servidores entre regiones - Entrevista de Fiamma con Clay Stone y Holly Longdale"
    },
    "summary": {
      "en": "Character Caps in WoW: Forever, Cross Region Servers - Fiamma Interview with Clay Stone and Holly Longdale...",
      "es": "Tapas de personajes en WoW: para siempre, servidores entre regiones - Entrevista de Fiamma con Clay Stone y Holly Longdale..."
    },
    "contentHtml": "\n            <div id=\"news-post-6acfade717ea48.68229717\" data-insert-ads=\"article\" data-zaf-dynamic=\"article\" data-units-dynamic=\"article\" data-zaf-slot=\"true\">Fiamma has interviewed Blizzard at PAX Australia 2026 on WoW: Forever to discuss character caps in WoW: Forever, the possibility of cross-region gameplay, and more!<br><br>At PAX Australia, many creators had the opportunity to interview Holly Longdale and Clay Stone. Fiamma has released her interview on her <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@FiammaCollects\" data-contiguous=\"true\" target=\"_blank\">YouTube Channel</a>.,<br><br><div class=\"wh-center\" style=\"text-align: -webkit-center;\"><div class=\"wh-youtube exclude-units lazy-load-background\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16 / 9; background: url(&quot;https://i.ytimg.com/vi/r0xvPeM4Ohw/sddefault.jpg&quot;); max-width: 800px;\"><a aria-label=\"Play\" class=\"wh-youtube-inner\" href=\"javascript:\" style=\"padding-top: 45%;\"><i class=\"fa fa-play-circle\"></i></a></div></div><div class=\"injected-ad-container\"><div class=\"htlad-desktop-dynamic-btf\"></div></div><br><br>We've summarized some of the key points below. <br><br><span class=\"large-text\">Cross Region</span><ul class=\"exclude-units\"><li><div data-markup-content-target=\"1\">There are technical challenges with cross-region.</div></li><li><div data-markup-content-target=\"1\">This is the first time they're attempting to go realmless, where players only need to choose the rulesets.</div></li><li><div data-markup-content-target=\"1\">This is working really well on the Beta, but this is as far as they can take it right now.</div></li><li><div data-markup-content-target=\"1\">It's not that they don't want to try it, but they need time.</div></li></ul><span class=\"large-text\">Character Caps</span><ul class=\"exclude-units\"><li><div data-markup-content-target=\"1\">They haven't announced what the character cap is at launch yet for WoW: Forever.</div></li><li><div data-markup-content-target=\"1\">There are technical limits on it.</div></li></ul><span class=\"large-text\">Porting Features to Retail</span><ul class=\"exclude-units\"><li><div data-markup-content-target=\"1\">When asked if there's a chance that Forever features such as the Transmog changes can come to Retail, Holly responds with an immediate \"yes\".</div></li><li><div data-markup-content-target=\"1\">They just have to talk about what's appropriate for each game.</div></li><li><div data-markup-content-target=\"1\">Holly will talk with Ion about it.</div></li></ul><span class=\"large-text\">Feedback</span><ul class=\"exclude-units\"><li><div data-markup-content-target=\"1\">They look at every venue for feedback: Reddit, videos, etc.</div></li><li><div data-markup-content-target=\"1\">For WoW: Forever, they listen everywhere: forums, social media, watching YouTube videos, YouTube comments. They are everywhere.</div></li><li><div data-markup-content-target=\"1\">When the big topics come up, they have heard of them.</div></li><li><div data-markup-content-target=\"1\">Then it comes to priority and how quickly they can get to stuff.</div></li><li><div data-markup-content-target=\"1\">It's also whether they agree it's right for the game.</div></li><li><div data-markup-content-target=\"1\">There are internal Blizzard employees who are massive collectors.</div></li><li><div data-markup-content-target=\"1\">Even on the Forever team, some developers play more Retail than Classic, so there's internal feedback as well.</div></li></ul><span class=\"large-text\">About the Devs</span><ul class=\"exclude-units\"><li><div data-markup-content-target=\"1\">Clay's favorite mount is a Dire Wolf, as he plays an Orc.</div></li><li><div data-markup-content-target=\"1\">Holly's favorite mount is the Friendship Fox for right now.</div></li><li><div data-markup-content-target=\"1\">Holly started playing at Launch and was in the WoW Beta.</div></li><li><div data-markup-content-target=\"1\">Clay started playing in 2006, just before the Burning Crusade.</div></li></ul><span class=\"large-text\">Art Style</span><ul class=\"last\"><li><div data-markup-content-target=\"1\">There's lots of training and mentoring.</div></li><li><div data-markup-content-target=\"1\">Forever is in a different art and training path than Retail.</div></li><li><div data-markup-content-target=\"1\">There's a lot of talent.</div></li></ul></div>\n            \n            <noscript>Fiamma has interviewed Blizzard at PAX Australia 2026 on WoW: Forever to discuss character caps in WoW: Forever, the possibility of cross-region gameplay, and more!<br /><br />At PAX Australia, many creators had the opportunity to interview Holly Longdale and Clay Stone. Fiamma has released her interview on her <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@FiammaCollects\" rel=\"nofollow\">YouTube Channel</a>.,<br /><br />We've summarized some of the key points below. <br /><br />Cross Region<br /><br /><ul><li>There are technical challenges with cross-region.</li><li>This is the first time they're attempting to go realmless, where players only need to choose the rulesets.</li><li>This is working really well on the Beta, but this is as far as they can take it right now.</li><li>It's not that they don't want to try it, but they need time.</li></ul><br /><br />Character Caps<br /><br /><ul><li>They haven't announced what the character cap is at launch yet for WoW: Forever.</li><li>There are technical limits on it.</li></ul><br /><br />Porting Features to Retail<br /><br /><ul><li>When asked if there's a chance that Forever features such as the Transmog changes can come to Retail, Holly responds with an immediate &quot;yes&quot;.</li><li>They just have to talk about what's appropriate for each game.</li><li>Holly will talk with Ion about it.</li></ul><br /><br />Feedback<br /><br /><ul><li>They look at every venue for feedback: Reddit, videos, etc.</li><li>For WoW: Forever, they listen everywhere: forums, social media, watching YouTube videos, YouTube comments. They are everywhere.</li><li>When the big topics come up, they have heard of them.</li><li>Then it comes to priority and how quickly they can get to stuff.</li><li>It's also whether they agree it's right for the game.</li><li>There are internal Blizzard employees who are massive collectors.</li><li>Even on the Forever team, some developers play more Retail than Classic, so there's internal feedback as well.</li></ul><br /><br />About the Devs<br /><br /><ul><li>Clay's favorite mount is a Dire Wolf, as he plays an Orc.</li><li>Holly's favorite mount is the Friendship Fox for right now.</li><li>Holly started playing at Launch and was in the WoW Beta.</li><li>Clay started playing in 2006, just before the Burning Crusade.</li></ul><br /><br />Art Style<br /><br /><ul><li>There's lots of training and mentoring.</li><li>Forever is in a different art and training path than Retail.</li><li>There's a lot of talent.</li></ul></noscript>            \n        ",
    "imageUrl": "https://wow.zamimg.com/uploads/blog/images/55712-character-caps-in-wow-forever-cross-region-servers-fiamma-interview-with-clay.jpg",
